<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="2JN" style="id">2 JOHN</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2JN 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2JN 1:1"/>
    The Elder,
    <verse eid="2JN 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    To the elect lady and her children, whom I love in truth—and not only I, but also all those who know the truth— 
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2JN 1:2"/>
    because of the truth* that abides in us and will be with us forever:
    <verse eid="2JN 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2JN 1:3"/>
    Grace, mercy, peace will be with us from God the Father and from Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and in love.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Walking According to God’s Commandments</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2JN 1:4"/>
    I rejoiced exceedingly that I had found some of your children walking in truth, just as we received a commandment from the Father. 
    <verse eid="2JN 1:4"/>
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2JN 1:5"/>
    And now I ask you, lady—not as though I were writing a new commandment to you, but the one that we have had from the beginning—that we should love one another. 
    <verse eid="2JN 1:5"/>
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2JN 1:6"/>
    And this is love, that we should walk according to His commandments. This is the commandment, just as you have heard from the beginning, so that you should walk in it.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Emergence of the Deceivers</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2JN 1:7"/>
    For many deceivers have gone out into the world, those who do not confess Jesus Christ as coming in the flesh. This is the deceiver and the antichrist. 
    <verse eid="2JN 1:7"/>
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2JN 1:8"/>
    Watch yourselves, so that you do not lose what we have worked for, but receive a full reward. 
    <verse eid="2JN 1:8"/>
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2JN 1:9"/>
    Everyone who goes beyond the bounds and does not abide in the teaching* of Christ does not have God. The one who abides in the teaching*—this one has both the Father and the Son. 
    <verse eid="2JN 1:9"/>
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2JN 1:10"/>
    If anyone comes to you and does not bring this teaching, do not receive him into your house, and do not offer him a greeting,* 
    <verse eid="2JN 1:10"/>
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2JN 1:11"/>
    because the one who offers him a greeting* participates in his evil deeds.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Farewell Greeting </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2JN 1:12"/>
    Although I have much to write to you, I do not wish to do so* by means of paper and ink, but I hope to come to you and to speak face to face,* so that our* joy may be made full.
    <verse eid="2JN 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2JN 1:13"/>
    The children of your elect sister greet you.*
    <verse eid="2JN 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">
    2 Some ancient manuscripts omit the prepositional phrase 
    <char style="it">because of the truth</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    9 Two ancient Greek manuscripts read 
    <char style="it">love </char>
    to achieve a degree of parallelism with 1 Jn. 4:16
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    9 Some ancient manuscripts insert at this point the genitive phrase 
    <char style="it">of Christ</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    10 Greek 
    <char style="it">and do not speak a greeting to him</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    11 Greek 
    <char style="it">because the one who speaks a greeting to him</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    12 The pro-verb construction 
    <char style="it">to do so</char>
     is supplied to the text based on context for the sake of clarity
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    12 Greek 
    <char style="it">mouth to mouth</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    12 Some ancient manuscripts read 
    <char style="it">your</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    13 Some ancient manuscripts insert
    <char style="it"> Amen </char>
    at the end of the verse
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2JN 1"/>
</usx>
